notes.notes:
[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added an option to remove blood and gore! You can find it in the Settings menu of both the Main Menu and the Pause Menu;
-Made new particle effects that appear when bullets hit flesh in the "no blood and gore" mode;
-Censored swear words, except for their first letter, so that only knowers will know;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Pursuit bounty being incorrectly shown in the display bar, when the wanted level is of 1 star;
-Pursuit music not starting if police pursuits end and then start again in less than a second;
-Pause Menu buttons not being highlighted reliably when hovering the mouse cursor on them;


[b]Português:[/b]

[b]Diversos:[/b]
-Adicionei uma opção para remover sangue e violência! Ela pode ser encontrada no menu de Configurações do Menu Principal e no menu de Configurações do Menu de Pause;
-Fiz novos efeitos que aparecem quando as balas atingem inimigos no modo "sem sangue e violência";
-Palavrões censurados, exceto a primeira letra deles, para que apenas os sabedores saibam;

[b]Bugs Corrigidos:[/b]
-Pontuação de perseguição sendo mostrada incorretamente na barra de perseguição, quando o nível de procurado é de 1 estrela;
-Música de perseguição não começando se a perseguição policial terminar e recomeçar em menos de um segundo;
-Botões do menu de pausa nem sempre sendo destacados ao passar o cursor do mouse sobre eles;

Added a Speedrun Mode! Start a new game and select the Speedrun Mode option to get it to work.

[b]Bugs Fixed:[/b]
-Language button in the main menu disappearing when the aspect ratio of your display is wider than 16:9;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-A new tutorial screen that explains where your vehicles are stored (the ones that are gifted to you when you save civilians in flying cages). The vehicles you earn are stored in the closest parking lot to your hideout, by the way. My apologies for not making this clear in the last update.
-A new toggle in the quality settings menu to disable tall grass, since it can be pretty demanding on slower computers;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Gifted cars having people in them;


[b]Portuguese:[/b]

[b]Adições:[/b]
-Uma nova tela de tutorial que explica onde seus veículos são guardados (os que você ganha ao salvar civis em gaiolas voadoras). Os veículos que você ganha ficam no estacionamento mais próximo de seu esconderijo. Me desculpe por não ter deixado isso claro na última atualização;
-Uma nova opção no menu de qualidade visual para desabilitar a grama animada, pois ela pode pesar um pouco em computadores fracos;

[b]Bugs Consertados:[/b]
-Carros do jogador tendo pessoas dentro;

[b]English:[/b]

[b]New activity:[/b] Civilian rescue! There are now flying cages carrying civilians around Copistan. Save the civilians and talk to the them, and you might get a reward!

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Tutorial Island disappearing when the draw distance settings are too low, leading the player to inevitably drown during the tutorial;
-Pedestrians no longer appearing in the smaller city since the drone enemy update;
-Issue with the portuguese interface: "Quality Settings" button not being displayed fully;

[b]Português:[/b]

[b]Nova atividade:[/b] resgate de civis! Agora existem gaiolas voadoras carregando civis por Copistan. Salve os civis e fale com eles para ser recompensado!

[b]Bugs Corrigidos:[/b]
-Ilha tutorial desaparecendo quando as configurações de distância estão muito baixas, fazendo o jogador morrer afogado inevitavelmente durante o tutorial;
-Pedestres não aparecendo na cidade menor desde o update que introduziu o inimigo drone;
-Problema com a interface em português: botão "Configurações Avançadas" não sendo exibido completamente;

Added a Brazilian Portuguese translation to the game! I had to change a lot of code to make the language changing system, so let me know if I accidentally broke anything.

Adicionei uma tradução para o português brasileiro ao jogo! Alterei muito código para fazer o sistema de mudança de linguagem, então me avisem se eu quebrei alguma coisa acidentalmente.

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added some important lines of dialogue;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Ammo boxes not spawning sniper rifle ammo when destroyed;
-Wanted level going up if you interact with the buttons of any weapon store in the proximity of a police officer;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Improved the Player's running animations (Kimo's arms were looking weirdly stiff);
-Added teleportation particle effects and sounds to the player when he steals a vehicle;
-Made a better water sound effect for the destroyed fire hydrant;
-Added more options to the secret cheat codes menu*;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Pedestrians getting scared for no reason when the player uses the pause menu;
-Pedestrians not getting scared of player driven tanks shooting;
-Pedestrians far away running in the wrong axis when scared;

[i]*You can access the secret cheat codes menu by pausing the game and typing a word that starts with the letter 'C'![/i]

A new enemy has been added: the morality drone. They roam the streets, scan both pedestrians and the player, and punish them if they find something wrong. They're very nimble during combat, so you better have a good aim!

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Replaced the rolling spikes trap in one of the cave Dungeons with a moving spiky wall;
-Increased the bounty requirements to increase wanted levels a bit;

[b]Bug and Mistake Fixes:[/b]
-Demolition mode tutorial showing up if you already saw it;
-Unintended blurring of particle effects from the police pursuit final boss, when motion blur is on;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added a camera shake intensity slider to the settings menu (which is in the pause menu);
-Tanks now smoke and burn when badly damaged, like cars in the game do;
-Player driven tanks now sink in the ocean;
-Added tank tread sounds to tanks when the player is driving them;
-Added driveable tanks to 3 of the military outposts;
-Made a new material for the rock platforms from the tutorial island, which were completely flat;

[b]Bug and Mistake Fixes:[/b]
-Enemy homing missiles not exploding when colliding with player driven vehicles;
-Tank driving inputs not being able to be remapped;
-Some tanks being lit incorrectly, looking much darker than intended;
-Player hair visible when inside a tank, and player driven tank being lit incorrectly;
-Player footsteps playing after pausing and then unpausing the game while driving a tank;
-New cave dungeon not counting towards the completion of the cave dungeons Steam achievement;
-My arena system breaks if the player beats a difficulty and then attempts to play the same difficulty again in the same session. I addressed this issue by preventing the player from attempting to play the same difficulty after they've beaten it during the same session. However, if you return to the main menu and reload the game, you'll be able to play the same difficulty again;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made a new cave Dungeon!
-Cut-scene loading times are around 90% faster now;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Player fall velocity increasing when not falling in some circumstances, making the player fall really fast nonsensically when that happens; 
-Key-card sound playing for a while even after being collected;

I recently noticed that two pictures were missing, and I have no idea how this happened, because in my repeated testing there were no pictures missing. But anyway, I'm sorry about those missing photos and for the really late update.

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Saves now include information about which dungeon teleporters have been activated; (sorry for not adding this earlier)
-The health bar now blinks when Kimo's health is under 50%;
-Getting damaged now shakes the camera a little;
-Added a compass to the minimap;

[b]Bug and Mistake Fixes:[/b]
-Added a rare photo and a cursed one to the open world;
-One of the photos in the second big dungeon not being counted on the map screen;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made particle effects for: car crashes, street lights and fire hydrants breaking; 
-Made more sound effects for vehicles crashes, in different intensities;
-Added camera shake to car crashes when driving;
-Made a particle effect for when flying cars are close to the ground;
-Made tutorial screens for both ground cars and flying cars;
-Building debris now also damage city enemies and pedestrians;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-When the player shoots nearby: Pedestrians not getting scared, and cops not initiating pursuits;
-Flying cars not sinking;
-Before getting the pistol: Weapon interface showing up if the game is paused and then unpaused;
-Before getting the pistol: Kimo's right hand shaped as if it's holding something;
-Menu buttons being highlighted incorrectly when using the mouse;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made and implemented a visual damage system on all ground vehicles (!);
-Building debris now damages outpost enemies;
-Made an interior for the military outpost building that was lacking it;

[b]BugFixes:[/b]
-Player being able to shoot in elevator rides;
-Slingshot ability causing dialogues to unfreeze time;
-Physics not activating reliably on objects on top of high up platforms;
-Buildings on top of buildings sometimes hanging out awkwardly after having their physics activated;
-Exploded car models sometimes not matching their model from before it exploded;
-Missiles not exploding when colliding with some types of grass floors;
-Military floor columns not emitting light;
-Inverted polygons in some of the buildings on high platforms, making them "see-through" from below;

[b]Steam Achievements have been added![/b]

 If you already achieved the things described in the achievements, you can get the achievements you earned upon loading the game in the city. Well, except for these achievements: SSS Combo, Arena Master, and Boss Beater. The reason why these 3 achievements won't be loaded is that I forgot to put the appropriate info about their actions in the save system, so there's nothing to load (oops!). So if you want to get these achievements you'll have to do the required feats a second time. If you have already beat all of the bosses before this update, you don't need to beat all of them again to earn the achievement, only the very last one.

In the next update I'll be focusing on polishing the game.

Misc:
-Made a new sound effect for important items (blueprints, keys, photos) to make it harder to miss them;
-Made it so police pursuits aren't initiated when destroying objects in the military bases;

 [b]Controller support is here![/b]
 If your controller doesn't work right away, please use the key mappings menu (accessible from the pause menu) to manually configure the buttons.
 I have personally found the game to be much harder to beat when using a controller, but I don't know if it's just me. Let me know if you found it to be too hard! And let me know if you'd like me to implement a form or aim assist and/or difficulty settings. 

[b]Controller Support Improvements:[/b]
-You can now use controller sticks to move the camera;
-Remade the interface system so you can navigate it using buttons or a mouse;
-In the input mappings menu, added a separate menu for changing controller inputs. Actions can now be mapped to two different buttons, so you can play using mouse + keyboard or controllers, without having to remap all inputs when switching to mouse + keyboard or to controllers;
-Fixed more instances of inputs that couldn't be mapped;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made a new purchase sound effect to replace the generic cash register sound;
-Made sounds for changing weapons;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Recoil going down instead of up if vertical camera rotation is inverted;
-Super Sprint effects playing while the player is driving a car, if the car was stolen while the Super Sprint is active;
-Secondary menus not closing if the game is unpaused;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added a chromatic aberration effect to the Slowdown ability;
-Made the pitch of sound effects lower when the Slowdown ability is active;
-Significantly reduced the energy cost of the Slowdown ability;
-Made an option in the controls menu for making melee attacks face the direction of the camera;
-Made voice sound effects for the last boss fight;
-Reduced the chance that the last boss drops health when damaged;
-Added hints to the loading screen;
-Added motion blur as an option in the quality settings menu (off by default);

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Flying cars not maintaining their speed if exited while in motion;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Self damage caused by explosions now deal half as much damage;
-Added a text to the weapon store that tells which button to press to leave;
-Made leveling the shotgun a bit slower;
-Reduced the amount of money awarded by engaging in police pursuits;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Player being able to get to the end of the game without beating the second big state building, if making progress in a certain order;
-Beating the 10th wanted level a second time not causing the main scene to be reloaded;
-Slide puzzle: input for initiating and closing the puzzle not being able to be remapped;
-Dungeon 1 classified document: input for continuing not being able to be remapped;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made tutorial slides for police pursuits and for the Mayhem activity;
-Big Dungeon 1: moved the checkpoint in the last floor to the entrance of the main boss room;
-Big Dungeon 1: reduced the amount of damage the player receives by the laser and the napalm attacks of the last boss, and also made it throw napalms at a slower rate;
-Reduced load time to the main scene by up to 15%;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Big Dungeon 1: main boss fight being able to be started from outside of the intended room, softlocking the game;
-Camera clipping outside of dungeon walls and ceilings in many instances;
-When falling into the water: player being respawned on top of their ragdoll, rather than on land;
-Player ragdoll not matching their equipped clothes at times;
-Pursuit level 10 boss: health bar showing incorrect value at times;
-Lemonade stand: dialogue after buying the sniper rifle causing the wepon store to open when pressing the input to display the next dialogue line;
-Second main Dungeon being able to be entered before the first;
-Big Dungeon 1: map showing a room that doesn't exist;
-Rocket launcher ammo count being loaded incorrectly at times;
-Last boss fight: police pursuit not being ended when the fight is initiated;
-Last boss fight: incorrect lightning and time of day if it's initiated at night (it's supposed to happen during the day);

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Completing cave dungeons now also contribute to opening the doors to the two main dungeons (the big state buildings);
-Increased the required completion to open the doors to the two main dungeons;
-Re-balanced how much certain accomplishments reduce Galaxy Brain's popularity;
-Made nights faster;
-Increased the default draw distance for normal buildings;

[b]Bug fixes:[/b]
-Dungeons looking darker at night, which doesn't make sense since they don't receive light from outside;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made a new clothing item to be purchased;
-Clothes now require that you collect pictures in order to be bought at the lemonade stands;
-Compressed a few overly large interface images in order to reduce load times;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Player melee animation not transitioning to the jump animation if the player jumps immediately after meleeing;
-Fixed many instances of pedestrians wandering to unintended places and walking into walls;
-AI driven buses clipping onto other AI cars;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added more dialogue to the dungeons;
-Made health and energy bars smaller, and attached them to the map;
-Spread chihuahua pictures throughout the world;
-Made sound effects for the entrance doors to the main Dungeons;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Slingshot ability momentum not ending when the player is standing still on the floor, making him slide awkwardly;
-Audio issues in the last cutscene;
-Missing text in the first dialogue in the hideout;
-Dungeon elevator "use" input not being able to be remapped;
-Dungeon teleporter "use" input not being able to be remapped;
-Dungeon elevators being able to be used without the player on them;
-Dungeon elevators not disabling player's animations when active;

[b]Dungeon 2 Improvements:[/b]
-Created new traps;
-Improved platforming rooms, adding those new traps where appropriate;
-Added the 2 new enemies from the Arena update;
-Improved the battle rooms, giving them more interesting shapes, and making them more dangerous;
-Merged some rooms that didn't need to be separated;
-Removed pointless corridors and repetitive rooms;
-Made a new power-up to be acquired;

Just some polish before overhauling the second big Dungeon, which will take around 10 or more days of work. Thank you for your patience!

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made tall grass, and spread it throughout the map (but I'm not quite happy with their placement yet);
-Updated the tutorial images with ones that have the current visuals of the game;
-Added input prompts for cars and flying cars, but not for tanks yet;
-Swapped which Outpost gives the Sniper Rifle blueprint, the Sniper Ammo Pack blueprint, and the Laser Rifle
 blueprint, in order to make the acquisition of the Sniper Rifle blueprint easier*;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Fixed a soft-locking bug triggered by destroying outpost buildings when they're too far away, since I didn't design them to be destroyed when the "demolition mode" isn't active. Now the outposts are always protected by force fields, which are deactivated once the player is within the distance that activates the "demolition mode";
-Reward stands not freezing time when the camera is focused on them, leaving the player vulnerable;
-Cop cars appearing in the wrong rotation, glitching out of the road, creating traffic jams and other issues;
-Gun store: scroll limits getting smaller on higher resolutions;
-Gun store: sniper rifle dialogue happening every time the gun store is closed in the same playthrough;

*[i]The Sniper Rifle blueprint is now on the city graveyard outpost, the Laser Rifle blueprint is now in the smaller mountain outpost,
and the Sniper Rifle Ammo Pack blueprint is now in the isolated graveyard outpost; [/i]

[b]Dungeon 1 Improvements:[/b]
-Created new traps;
-Improved platforming rooms, adding those new traps where appropriate;
-Improved battle rooms, giving them more interesting shapes, and making them more dangerous;
-Merged some rooms that didn't need to be separated;
-Removed pointless corridors and repetitive rooms;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Player's animations glitching when the player walks over small ledges;
-Gun store: Catnip's dialogue being interrupted when hovering the mouse on different items;
-Gun store: Catnip's dialogue being partially displayed when closing and opening the store;

Just polishing the visuals a bit before making major improvements to the main Dungeons.

-Improved texture work for the mountains;
-Added a bit more vegetation;
-Increased distant fog density at night;
-Made ocean color darker at night and decreased ocean saturation overall;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Added crowd sounds to the Arena;
-Added a lemonade stand in the smaller city, and another in the Arena;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Melee cops interrupting their chase when the player is in the air;
-Arena: pursuits being initiated during the arena activity;
-Arena: small spider robots getting stuck in the mecha elevators;
-Traffic: fixed many instances where AI cars glitch their way out of the road;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-A new clothing item. I like it better than the previous Arena reward, so it replaced the reward;
-Clothing can now be purchased at the lemonade stands where Catnip sells guns;
-Catnip now talks at the lemonade stands, describing the weapons; Also, a new dialogue was added for when the player buys the Sniper Rifle;
-Added facial expressions to Catnip's models on cutscenes;
-Added facial expressions to Catnip's dialogue images, and improved Kimo's dialogue images;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Weapon store menu: scroll up and scroll down inputs not being able to be remapped;
-Items being highlighted incorrectly in the weapon store menu;
-Interface: demolition bar showing up and not disappearing after being spawned near some military bases that have been destroyed;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-New activity: the Arena! You can find it in the island that doesn't have a city (it still needs some polish though);
-A stronger variant of the quadruped mecha, which has an additional gun;
-A stronger variant of the biped mecha, which requires a different strategy to beat;
-A new items system for future collectible powerups or clothes;
-A new powerup you can win at the Arena;
-New clothes you can win at the Arena;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Last boss fight not being initiated; (I'm really sorry for this bug, I only noticed it now)
-Bullet casing sounds causing audio count limit issues;
-Draw distance of some types of object not being able to be customized in the quality settings menu;
-Fixed more instances of reward objects (experience orbs and currency) colliding incorrectly when an enemy is killed;

As an apology for breaking the last boss fight in the last update (it's fixed in this update), [b]here's a secret: if you type "chihuahua" in the pause menu, a secret cheat codes menu will appear![/b]

My apologies for another small update. I've been remaking some promotional material, but I'm almost done. But next in my list is adding a battle arena activity, so you can look forward to that!

[b]Wanted level 10 Boss Polish:[/b]
-Fixed bug where it floats in the air in some cases;
-Laser attack: It now destroys cars and kills people; New particle effects added; It now shakes the camera when close;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Interface icons for locations appearing distractingly big in the first frame they appear;
-Reward objects (especially experience orbs and currency) colliding incorrectly when an enemy is killed;
-Fixed bug where experience orbs collided with concrete debris, causing very aggressive collision issues;
-Some concrete debris colliding incorrectly;
-Homing Missile Mecha's debris also colliding incorrectly;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Improved the Combo system, which now: Indicates the ways the player killed enemies, awards XP, and displays a rating for the combo once it's finished.
I'm still thinking about whether the combo system should work on civilians, so it only works on enemies that fight back for now.
-Increased draw distance limit for buildings in the Quality Settings Menu;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Enemy tanks destroying lots of buildings off-screen during pursuits, causing extreme frame rate drops;
-One of the doors in the first big dungeon unable to be opened from the other side, making traversal bothersome;
-Slide puzzles repeating the unlock sound unnecessarily;
-Camera going through some military buildings;

Hey, everybody! Unfortunately, I won't be able to work on the game from 03/08/23 (march 8) to 03/18/23 (march 18). Anyway, here are the update notes:

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Polished the city some more;
-Improved car instantiation, making the roads livelier*;
-Added a slider to the Quality Settings menu to adjust the max traffic car count;
-Added a splash effect for when the player falls in the water;
-Made some changes to the post processing effects;

[b]Bugs Fixed:[/b]
-Cops walking on the sea, close to the smaller city;

*[i]However, with more cars, the bugs with my traffic system (and there are many) will be more noticeable. I'll address these bugs when I'm back.[/i]

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Flying cars can now also destroy buildings, provided they're flying fast enough;
-Increased maximum flying height for flying cars;
-Player driven vehicles hitting buildings now also get damaged; (but not visually, yet)
-Made a bump map for the building details;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Some enemy missiles not destroying vehicles;
-Flying car inputs not being able to be remapped;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-Added down-force to the cars, to make handling better at high speeds;
-Cars can now destroy buildings. A lighter car will need more speed in order to damage a building than a heavier one;
-Added cleanable mess to the Hideout, since Catnip is supposed to be messy;
-Added distance fog, but it's not as good as it should be at night yet;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Fixed the broken draw distance of miscellaneous objects for good;
-Increased the maximum draw distance of miscellaneous objects in the quality settings menu;

Apologies for another late update. Detailing the buildings is more work than it might seem, due to the fact that they're destructible.

[b]Visual polish:[/b]
-Detailed most of the building models;
-Added vegetation to the whole map;

[b]Bug fixes:[/b]
-Fixed bug that made explosion sounds from military base objects overlap, which made them really loud;
-Fixed bug that broke the vegetation culling system after opening and closing the weapon store;

I've been modelling details for the buildings in the game, but it's not in this update. I interrupted what I was doing in order to fix some rather bad bugs. But you can look forward to more detailed buildings in the next update!

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Nerfed the upgraded shotguns;
-Fixed some issues with the Player's animation transitions;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Energy generators from dungeons not being damaged by explosions;
-Fast enemies that are far away not being damaged by sniper bullets and laser beams;
-Old pedestrians (the blocky ones) appearing in the smaller city, causing many issues;
-Player's free falling animation not ending if the player hits the ground in certain ways;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-Made and implemented a headshot sound effect;
-Made and implemented an animation for when the player is in the air after using the Slingshot skill;

[b]General Polish:[/b]
-Fixed bug where Kimo appears levitating during some of the conversations at the hideout;
-Fixed bug where Kimo is able to aim with his arm during conversations;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-A new cave, which has a new boss fight and a new song(!). It is located in the island that doesn't have roads;
-Made and implemented a sound effect for electricity generators;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Progress inside of dungeons and caves not being saved properly;
-Cave map icons not changing in some cases after a cave is beaten;
-Ocean sounds sometimes playing while inside of dungeons or caves;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-Headshots! (took this long to add this obvious feature because of difficulty balance considerations);
-New character models implemented on the cutscenes;
-Dialogue images now feature the new character models;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Player bullets now home in on moving targets (provided the targets were accurately shot at), to make aiming more reliable;
-Fixed the following bugs I accidentally created in the last update: drone powerup not shooting, incorrect zombie and player death sounds, dash kick animation not playing; 

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Cave generators instantiating dozens of explosions upon being destroyed by shotgun hits, creating an ear violating sound;
-Bullets vanishing in the battle rooms located in the caves;

The new character models are here!

[b]Additions:[/b]
-All gameplay character models replaced with the new ones; (the cutscene ones haven't been replaced yet)
-Improved Kimo's jumping and idle animations;
-Tweaked other animations;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Gas station pumps not being damaged by bullets;

Apologies for another late update, I have been experimenting with remodelling character models. I just made the hard decision to remake all of the character models, so the next update should be a bit late too, as this will take at least a week of work. The beautiful people who have bought the game seem to not care so much about the character models, so I'm sorry to all of you who would rather see more content instead of visual polish, but the blocky characters are making it too hard to market the game. Thank you for your patience!

[b]Additions:[/b]
-A Slingshot Race activity added to the new city;
-A Mayhem activity added to the new city;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-Made a brute force option to improve how tall buildings crumble when they get destroyed at the base, but it can be VERY demanding on a mid range cpu, so I'm making it optional until I optimize it enough. To turn it on: [i]Pause > Settings > Advanced Settings > "Physics" tab >[/i] check the "Tall Building Crumble" toggle;
-Reduced volume of wood debris sounds;

[b]Misc:[/b]
-If the player dies in a military base, they'll be spawned next to it when the scene is reloaded;
-If the player dies in a cave and there are no checkpoints inside, they'll be spawned at the entrance when the scene is reloaded;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Saves made on older versions of the game not being loaded correctly, causing important scripts not to work, making the player always float on the ground;
-When a save is loaded: Player needlessly being spawned inside of a dungeon;
-Flying police vans instantiating an unlimited amount of cops;
-Biped Mecha's homing missile not exploding when colliding with cave walls;
-Some concrete debris sounds not playing in the new city;
-Concrete debris sounds not playing correctly in general;
-Some animated outdoors not working in the new city;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-The map has been expanded! The expanded portion of the map doesn't have stuff to do yet, like dungeons or activities, and it isn't as polished as it should be, but making it was a lot of work. Apologies for the delayed update.

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-"Shoot" and "change weapon" inputs not being able to be remapped on a generic controller or on Steam Deck buttons; (Steam Deck users: please let me know if it's actually fixed!)
-Slingshot direction inputs not being able to be remapped;
-Player's right arm aiming at the target at weird angles;
-Player being able to shoot in the hideout;
-NPC cars teleporting when correcting their direction;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-Bullet casings now come out of the player guns;
-Bullet casing sounds;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
-Suicidal pedestrians;
-Cars not stopping for pedestrians;
-Reduced issue of AI cars going through other AI cars;
-Car smoke and fire particles going up on their local up axis, as opposed to the world up axis;

[b]Additions:[/b]
-New activity: Mayhem!
-Added 3 Mayhem activities;
-Destroying military bases and beating activities now gives chihuahua pictures as rewards*, in addition to money and experience;

[b]Bug Fixes:[/b]
